From 0892852c8310fda326aa0a5c15a8adae36602b36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 21:29:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Make be96u-only buildable from a clean checkout: drop
 deprecated/conflicting sources

Deleted uncommitted in the build clone's working tree (so every RT-BE96U image was
built with them gone) but never committed -- a clean checkout fails to build. Commit
the removals so the branch builds reproducibly:
- iptables-1.4.x extensions that #include kernel netfilter headers absent from this
  tree (won't compile): ROUTE/ip6t_ROUTE, account, geoip, webstr, TOS, TRIGGER, ipp2p,
  tos, web, webmon/ip6t_webmon, xt_ethport.
- bundled ifaddrs.c in libusbmuxd/minidlna/miniupnpd/wsdd2: conflict with glibc
  getifaddrs; the packages use the system implementation.
Not model-specific, not a Reaper feature. Mirrors rt-be86u commit 897be9cfb3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
